ication impact. Since we need to be systematic, we could challenge Agent 1's weighting, perhaps argue that communication difficulty is a serious safety issue, especially for long-distance flights, and that Candidate B's stress resilience and technical competence may outweigh C's communication issues. Or we could ask Agent 1 for more detail about C's communication difficulty. But we can also bring up Candidate D's responsibility and problem solving. However, D has hot temper and know-it-all attitude.\n\nWe need to produce a public message with a vote. Let's decide: I think Candidate B might be a better overall fit because stress resilience and conscientiousness are crucial, and while B has some interpersonal issues, they are less severe than C's communication difficulty which could affect cockpit coordination. So I will propose Candidate B as my provisional recommendation, referencing facts: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, but also note concerns about nasty remarks and uncooperative behavior. I will argue that stress resilience and technical competence are more critical.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 1's point: they recommended C. I will say I see the strengths but have concerns about communication difficulty that could impact safety, and I think B's stress handling and technical skills make B a stronger candidate.\n\nThus public message: state recommendation Candidate B, refer to Agent 1's recommendation, give evidence, explain.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
